<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Orléans-Longueville</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th century–<a href="/years/1707">1707</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Orléans-Longueville were a French noble family descended from Jean de Dunois, the Bastard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a> and companion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a>. Dukes of Longueville from 1505, they acquired the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neuchatel">Neuchâtel</a> by marriage in 1504 and ruled it until the line died out with Marie de Nemours in 1707, when the estates chose the King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> as their sovereign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-orleans-longueville.jpg" alt="House of Orléans-Longueville" width="208" height="365" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Songsblame · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coats_of_arms_of_the_Dukes_of_Longueville.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
